   "MatterHistoryActionName": "elected",
   "MatterHistoryActionText": "The Rules, Confirmations, and Public Elections Committee recommended the nominees. The President called for an election to fill one vacancy on the Metro Animal Care and Control Commission for a representative from a local nonprofit organization dedicated to animal welfare. Nominations previously made were Brandon Dyce and Becky Carter. The following vote was taken on the nominated candidates: Brandon Dyce (19): Suara, Allen, Kimbrough, Toombs, Gamble, Harrell, Hancock, Webb, Eslick, Evans, Bradford, Huffman, Vo, Preptit, Benton, Ellis, Sepulveda, Styles, and Ewing; Becky Carter (14): Evans-Segall, Hill, Cortese, Parker, Capp, Benedict, Gregg, Cash, Druffel, Johnston, Nash, Rutherford, Lee, and Spain; Abstain (0). The president declared that Brandon Dyce was elected to the Commission.",
